{
    "background_story": "Charles, a British aristocrat, was known for his extravagant lifestyle and love of Indian culture. During his travels to India, he was fascinated by the grandeur of the maharajas and their opulent palaces. He became fast friends with the Maharaja of Rajasthan, who took him under his wing and taught him the intricacies of royal protocol. Charles was particularly drawn to the majestic architecture and stunning artwork of the maharaja's palace. He spent years collecting rare Indian artifacts and eventually built his own 'Maharaja's Palace' in the English countryside, a testament to his love of Indian heritage. Charles's estate became a popular destination for those seeking a taste of India's regal splendor, and he was often referred to as the 'Maharaja of England' due to his lavish lifestyle and love of all things Indian.",
